{
    "background_story": "Dexter was a brilliant but hapless scientist who had a knack for turning even the most promising experiments into catastrophes. His lab was a testament to his creative genius, but also to his disastrous lack of attention to detail. One fateful day, Dexter attempted to create a revolutionary new fuel source, but his concoction ended up exploding in a spectacular fashion, destroying half the lab and covering everything in a sticky, green goo. The incident became infamous in scientific circles, with many regarding it as one of the most epic failures in recent history. Despite his catastrophically bad luck, Dexter refused to give up, convinced that his next experiment would be the one that changed the world. His colleagues, however, made sure to keep a fire extinguisher handy whenever he was working on a new project.",
